codex
Stage timing shows the current FP16 projection kernel is the largest cost for `dim=384` (`~2.1 ms` at `N=768`, `~4.0 ms` at `N=1024`). The `bmm` contraction itself is only about `0.5-1.1 ms`, so the main opportunity is fusing or improving the input normalization/projection work.
